00:20:41,185 --> 00:20:42,625
-Where do we find this group?
-Someone tell him!

265
00:20:42,705 --> 00:20:43,665
Where can I find this club?
Please tell me.

266
00:20:43,745 --> 00:20:44,865
I need help ASAP!

267
00:20:44,945 --> 00:20:45,825
Where should I go?

268
00:20:45,905 --> 00:20:47,625
THE CROW CLUB

269
00:21:03,265 --> 00:21:04,145
Nugget!

270
00:21:06,425 --> 00:21:07,745
Like this. Spread your wings like this.

271
00:21:08,745 --> 00:21:10,865
Come on. Nugget! Nugget! Nugget!

272
00:21:16,465 --> 00:21:18,865
You think Linda won't see it?

273
00:21:20,545 --> 00:21:22,385
What did you take pity on
and bring home this time?

274
00:21:22,465 --> 00:21:24,505
Hey! Where are you going?

275
00:21:24,585 --> 00:21:26,385
You and that chick
will both get kicked out.

276
00:21:26,465 --> 00:21:29,025
Hey, are you really

277
00:21:29,105 --> 00:21:32,065
going to leave it outside
in the wind and rain?

278
00:21:32,145 --> 00:21:34,065
You heartless jerk.

279
00:21:35,825 --> 00:21:37,625
You named the chick "Nugget."

280
00:21:37,705 --> 00:21:39,065
I'm sure it'll grow up just fine.

281
00:21:40,425 --> 00:21:41,905
Mimi!

282
00:21:42,505 --> 00:21:43,425
Mimi!

283
00:21:43,945 --> 00:21:45,305
Mimi, where are you?

284
00:21:45,865 --> 00:21:47,625
Mi… Hey, where are you going?

285
00:21:47,705 --> 00:21:50,265
A supplier's waiting out back.
Go get the delivery.

286
00:21:50,865 --> 00:21:52,385
I'm going right now.

287
00:21:52,465 --> 00:21:54,065
-Then go!
-But…

288
00:21:54,585 --> 00:21:55,825
Hurry. You're keeping them waiting.

289
00:21:55,905 --> 00:21:58,385
-What's wrong with you?
-My back… My back hurts.

290
00:21:58,465 --> 00:21:59,585
Go!

291
00:22:00,105 --> 00:22:02,465
I'm going. I'm going now.

292
00:22:02,545 --> 00:22:03,825
You go ahead, Linda.

293
00:22:03,905 --> 00:22:06,665
I'll see you off…
until you're out of sight.

294
00:22:06,745 --> 00:22:09,025
Come on! You're keeping
them waiting. Hurry!

295
00:22:09,665 --> 00:22:10,905
What's with her?

296
00:22:18,505 --> 00:22:20,825
Tangmo! Can you get the delivery for me?

297
00:22:20,905 --> 00:22:23,905
Please. I have to hide Nugget.

298
00:22:23,985 --> 00:22:26,625
Please, just for a sec. Thank you.

299
00:22:29,705 --> 00:22:31,945
Vann, you go.

300
00:22:32,025 --> 00:22:34,465
No, I'm researching universities.

301
00:22:35,145 --> 00:22:36,425
You go ahead.

302
00:22:37,865 --> 00:22:39,225
Fine. I'll go.

303
00:23:00,065 --> 00:23:01,065
Yoyeh?

304
00:23:02,505 --> 00:23:03,865
Oh, Tangmo.

305
00:23:04,825 --> 00:23:06,425
Long time no see.

306
00:23:06,505 --> 00:23:07,505
How have you been?

307
00:23:08,265 --> 00:23:09,865
What are you doing here?

308
00:23:11,625 --> 00:23:14,185
I'm delivering beer to The Crow Club.

309
00:23:14,905 --> 00:23:17,065
Today's my first day on the job.

310
00:23:18,425 --> 00:23:19,825
I'm glad to see you.

311
00:23:19,905 --> 00:23:21,945
Once you're done, you can leave.

312
00:23:22,025 --> 00:23:23,745
And don't come here again.

313
00:23:25,465 --> 00:23:27,105
Wait, Tangmo.

314
00:23:31,465 --> 00:23:33,505
Uh… It's just that…

315
00:23:33,585 --> 00:23:35,065
Sis hasn't paid for the order yet.

316
00:23:36,585 --> 00:23:37,585
Here's the bill.

317
00:23:38,945 --> 00:23:40,865
You haven't changed one damn bit.

318
00:23:40,945 --> 00:23:42,785
I'll tell Sis to transfer the money.

319
00:23:43,385 --> 00:23:46,705
As for you, leave and don't come back.

320
00:23:56,065 --> 00:23:57,905
Oh, I'm sweating.

321
00:23:58,505 --> 00:24:00,545
-Can you throw this away for me, Talay?
-Sis…

322
00:24:01,585 --> 00:24:04,345
I'm begging you.
Don't use this beer supplier again.

323
00:24:04,425 --> 00:24:05,265
I don't like them.

324
00:24:05,345 --> 00:24:07,545
He's just delivering beer.
Why don't you like him?

325
00:24:08,305 --> 00:24:10,625
I don't like the delivery guy's face.

326
00:24:10,705 --> 00:24:12,065
-I can't stand him.
-Hey!

327
00:24:13,505 --> 00:24:15,425
He's just making a delivery.

328
00:24:15,505 --> 00:24:16,785
Why do you hate him so much?

329
00:24:21,465 --> 00:24:22,585
Hey, Sis.

330
00:24:23,225 --> 00:24:24,945
You asked, and he wouldn't answer.

331
00:24:25,465 --> 00:24:27,345
I bet those two have a past.

332
00:24:28,585 --> 00:24:29,705
A past?

333
00:24:31,585 --> 00:24:32,625
A past.

334
00:24:33,145 --> 00:24:34,505
What a shame.

335
00:24:34,585 --> 00:24:39,465
If I'd gone down there earlier,
I would've seen Tangmo's past.

336
00:24:39,985 --> 00:24:41,105
Mimi!

337
00:24:41,185 --> 00:24:43,225
-Hey! Don't touch me!
-Calm down.

338
00:24:43,305 --> 00:24:45,985
-Enough.
-Talay, look! He's picking on me!

339
00:24:46,065 --> 00:24:48,265
Enough! I have a headache.

340
00:24:48,345 --> 00:24:49,865
Stop messing around.

341
00:24:50,465 --> 00:24:52,305
God, all this noise.

342
00:24:52,385 --> 00:24:54,265
You do nothing all day.

343
00:24:54,865 --> 00:24:55,945
This one's a total nutcase.

344
00:24:56,825 --> 00:25:00,145
And this one… is hotheaded
and always gets violent.

345
00:25:02,385 --> 00:25:04,465
And don't you smile.

346
00:25:04,545 --> 00:25:06,025
You're no different.

347
00:25:06,105 --> 00:25:08,145
You're supposed to be the leader,

348
00:25:08,705 --> 00:25:10,425
but you're so unpredictable.

349
00:25:11,025 --> 00:25:11,865
And this girl…

350
00:25:14,465 --> 00:25:15,785
You're fine.

351
00:25:15,865 --> 00:25:17,065
As for Phatee…

352
00:25:18,985 --> 00:25:19,825
You…

353
00:25:21,025 --> 00:25:22,025
Look at that guy.

354
00:25:23,665 --> 00:25:25,785
Won't talk, won't listen,
won't do anything.

355
00:25:25,865 --> 00:25:29,265
I'm taking all of you
to a psychiatrist once and for all.

356
00:25:30,945 --> 00:25:33,425
Sis, why do you only yell at us?

357
00:25:33,505 --> 00:25:34,745
You never yell at Vann.

358
00:25:34,825 --> 00:25:36,305
Exactly, Bro.

359
00:25:36,385 --> 00:25:38,425
And you keep calling to check on Vann.

360
00:25:38,505 --> 00:25:40,625
He's graduated from college, Sis.

361
00:25:40,705 --> 00:25:41,545
He's not a kid anymore.

362
00:25:41,625 --> 00:25:42,625
Why?

363
00:25:43,385 --> 00:25:46,865
Just because I don't yell at Vann
doesn't mean I'm not worried about him.

364
00:25:46,945 --> 00:25:50,025
I'm just less worried
about him than you guys.

365
00:25:50,585 --> 00:25:52,305
At least he has a goal.

366
00:25:52,385 --> 00:25:54,385
What goals do you guys have in life?

367
00:25:54,465 --> 00:25:56,825
Tell me. Do you have a goal in life?

368
00:25:56,905 --> 00:25:59,065
I want to be Talay's wife.

369
00:25:59,145 --> 00:26:00,865
Take it easy. Easy.

370
00:26:01,945 --> 00:26:02,985
Mimi.

371
00:26:04,345 --> 00:26:06,465
See? I have a goal now.

372
00:26:07,745 --> 00:26:09,185
Goals are meant to be pursued.

373
00:26:09,265 --> 00:26:10,185
Stop!

374
00:26:20,225 --> 00:26:21,305
-Hey.
-Hmm?

375
00:26:22,025 --> 00:26:23,945
I thought our bar was weird enough,

376
00:26:24,545 --> 00:26:26,225
but the customers are even weirder.

377
00:26:26,745 --> 00:26:27,865
Sis, look over there.

378
00:26:28,985 --> 00:26:33,425
What kind of weirdo brings a typewriter
to type at a bar every single day?

379
00:26:33,945 --> 00:26:36,865
But… I've never seen him type anything.

380
00:26:38,345 --> 00:26:39,425
Just typing away at nothing?

381
00:26:39,505 --> 00:26:40,425
Yeah.

382
00:26:41,785 --> 00:26:45,385
At first, I thought he might like Sis.

383
00:26:45,465 --> 00:26:48,225
Or if not, he must like you.

384
00:26:49,265 --> 00:26:50,985
But then I realized that wasn't it.

385
00:26:51,065 --> 00:26:52,905
I think he likes me more.

386
00:26:53,505 --> 00:26:54,465
Mimi.

387
00:26:55,065 --> 00:26:57,385
I'm begging you. Tone it down a little.

388
00:26:57,465 --> 00:26:58,865
You don't have to get jealous.

389
00:27:29,985 --> 00:27:33,545
Sun, when the hell are you sending
the manuscript?

390
00:27:33,625 --> 00:27:36,105
I've put my neck on the line for you
to push back the deadline.

391
00:27:36,185 --> 00:27:37,145
I can't do it anymore.

392
00:27:37,665 --> 00:27:39,305
Come on, I'm almost done writing it.

393
00:27:39,385 --> 00:27:40,545
I'll definitely send it to you.

394
00:27:41,185 --> 00:27:42,025
When you say that,

395
00:27:42,105 --> 00:27:44,225
I'm sure you haven't
written a single word.

396
00:27:44,305 --> 00:27:47,465
Are you really going to
let yourself fall off this far?

397
00:27:47,545 --> 00:27:50,985
You used to be a romance novelist
with sky-high sales.

398
00:27:51,065 --> 00:27:52,505
Don't say "used to" to me.

399
00:27:52,585 --> 00:27:53,785
I still am.

400
00:27:54,305 --> 00:27:55,785
But if you're still stuck,

401
00:27:55,865 --> 00:27:57,425
"used to" is exactly what you'll be.

402
00:27:57,505 --> 00:28:00,665
Look. Hurry up and find some material
to write about.

403
00:28:00,745 --> 00:28:02,665
The publisher can't give you
much more time.

404
00:28:03,425 --> 00:28:05,065
Otherwise,
they'll terminate your contract.

405
00:28:25,185 --> 00:28:26,465
The usual?

406
00:28:30,665 --> 00:28:32,385
Any other requests?

407
00:28:35,465 --> 00:28:36,665
I'd like to request you.

408
00:28:47,025 --> 00:28:50,625
They say The Crow Club takes secret jobs
and can solve any problem,

409
00:28:50,705 --> 00:28:53,025
as long as the client has money.

410
00:28:53,545 --> 00:28:55,465
Is that true or just bragging?

411
00:28:57,865 --> 00:28:59,665
Did you secretly research the club?

412
00:29:00,585 --> 00:29:03,865
You must've seen it
in the runaways' community chat.

413
00:29:04,825 --> 00:29:06,985
I just happened to hear about it.

414
00:29:07,065 --> 00:29:09,505
So, can you really solve anything?

415
00:29:11,665 --> 00:29:12,905
Pretty much anything.

416
00:29:14,265 --> 00:29:16,265
But anything beyond human ability,

417
00:29:16,825 --> 00:29:19,425
like making things disappear
or bringing people back to life,

418
00:29:20,265 --> 00:29:22,265
or playing wizard,
we don't take jobs like that.

419
00:29:23,065 --> 00:29:24,905
We don't write novels for hire either.

420
00:29:25,425 --> 00:29:27,265
That would be deceiving consumers.

421
00:29:46,945 --> 00:29:49,425
Smoking will make you die sooner.

422
00:30:07,945 --> 00:30:10,425
Candy can kill you sooner too
if you eat too much.

423
00:30:12,305 --> 00:30:14,825
True, but at least it's sweet.

424
00:30:19,745 --> 00:30:22,625
Then, what about hiring someone
to get them to fall in love,

425
00:30:22,705 --> 00:30:24,305
or hiring someone to be your lover?

426
00:30:24,825 --> 00:30:27,825
Are those within the scope
of jobs this club takes?

427
00:30:32,225 --> 00:30:34,665
You're the perfect material.

428
00:30:35,345 --> 00:30:39,545
You check all the boxes
for the character in my novel.

429
00:30:43,185 --> 00:30:44,465
I want to hire you.

430
00:30:48,505 --> 00:30:53,945
Mr. Writer, in this bar,
I'm the last person you should hire.

431
00:30:54,945 --> 00:30:56,545
Because I don't believe in "love"

432
00:30:56,625 --> 00:30:59,585
or the silly "destiny"
in your romance novels.

433
00:31:00,265 --> 00:31:01,345
Understand?

434
00:31:51,985 --> 00:31:54,705
-Can I take a photo with you?
-Sorry, but no.

435
00:32:08,585 --> 00:32:09,745
Mr. Singer,

436
00:32:10,865 --> 00:32:12,585
I really like the song you sang.

437
00:32:12,665 --> 00:32:13,985
Did you write it yourself?

438
00:32:17,345 --> 00:32:19,705
I'm forming a band to make our debut.

439
00:32:20,385 --> 00:32:22,425
And I'd like you to join the band.

440
00:32:26,585 --> 00:32:27,465
Sorry.

441
00:32:28,665 --> 00:32:29,585
Wait.

442
00:32:30,305 --> 00:32:31,265
Uh…

443
00:32:31,865 --> 00:32:32,745
How about this?

444
00:32:36,305 --> 00:32:38,185
We can start by being friends.

445
00:32:40,385 --> 00:32:41,665
I'm Ranne.

446
00:32:42,345 --> 00:32:44,345
I'm Ranne.

447
00:32:50,945 --> 00:32:54,385
You've seen us
in the label's trainee clips, right?

448
00:32:57,745 --> 00:32:58,825
Never.

449
00:32:59,505 --> 00:33:00,585
Sorry.

450
00:33:22,705 --> 00:33:23,945
Hello, Kao.

451
00:33:24,465 --> 00:33:25,785
We found him,

452
00:33:25,865 --> 00:33:28,025
the fifth member
to redo the audition with us.

453
00:33:28,865 --> 00:33:30,705
You'll meet him soon.

454
00:33:31,465 --> 00:33:34,145
I believe this time,

455
00:33:34,225 --> 00:33:35,945
my band will actually make our debut.

456
00:33:52,265 --> 00:33:53,225
Ranne.

457
00:34:09,425 --> 00:34:10,465
Hey, you!

458
00:34:18,744 --> 00:34:19,665
Hey!

459
00:34:21,585 --> 00:34:23,185
You pervert! What the hell are you doing?

460
00:34:27,665 --> 00:34:29,185
Vann, what are you doing?

461
00:34:29,905 --> 00:34:31,025
Lonely, little Bro?

462
00:34:31,744 --> 00:34:33,465
Can you guys stop hanging out in my room?

463
00:34:33,985 --> 00:34:35,824
My room isn't a living room.

464
00:34:36,344 --> 00:34:37,824
Your room's the most fun.

465
00:34:37,905 --> 00:34:39,025
It's the youngest one's room.

466
00:34:39,105 --> 00:34:40,665
The youngest, huh?

467
00:34:43,065 --> 00:34:47,264
Come on, we're just
looking for a place to hang out.

468
00:34:48,025 --> 00:34:50,505
You're just looking for somewhere
to eat and make me clean up.

469
00:34:51,824 --> 00:34:54,304
Hey! What are you doing?

470
00:34:54,385 --> 00:34:56,225
Tangmo, enough. Stop messing with him.

471
00:34:56,905 --> 00:34:59,345
So? How was your job today?

472
00:34:59,425 --> 00:35:01,705
Sis said you charged several times more.

473
00:35:02,225 --> 00:35:03,625
Got enough money for Japan yet?

474
00:35:05,545 --> 00:35:07,145
How much could I possibly charge?

475
00:35:07,225 --> 00:35:09,265
I only got a little extra
for getting punched.

476
00:35:10,665 --> 00:35:12,545
I was so fucking unlucky today.

477
00:35:13,185 --> 00:35:14,185
Just hang in there.

478
00:35:14,705 --> 00:35:17,225
The money for your
Engineering Master's in Japan

479
00:35:17,305 --> 00:35:18,785
is in the millions, right?

480
00:35:19,385 --> 00:35:21,705
If some well-connected kid
hadn't taken the scholarship last time,

481
00:35:22,305 --> 00:35:24,385
I wouldn't be with a bunch
of weirdos like you guys.

482
00:35:24,465 --> 00:35:25,985
Huh? Weirdos?

483
00:35:26,065 --> 00:35:28,425
-Tangmo, get him!
-Weirdos? Eat this popcorn!

484
00:35:30,025 --> 00:35:31,065
I'm not stopping him either.

485
00:35:31,145 --> 00:35:32,585
It's all over the place.

486
00:35:42,025 --> 00:35:44,785
A client will come discuss
a job with you tomorrow.

487
00:35:44,865 --> 00:35:46,825
So meet at the club at ten sharp.

488
00:35:48,185 --> 00:35:50,745
Jobs mean money. Money means jobs.

489
00:35:50,825 --> 00:35:52,345
Our club is pretty damn popular.

490
00:36:05,545 --> 00:36:06,745
I've got a job too.

491
00:36:07,385 --> 00:36:08,505
Me too.

492
00:36:10,025 --> 00:36:12,425
-Did you get one too?
-Yeah.

493
00:36:12,505 --> 00:36:13,465
Yeah.

494
00:36:14,145 --> 00:36:15,025
What?

495
00:36:15,545 --> 00:36:17,505
Is that the only word you know?

496
00:36:45,865 --> 00:36:47,625
Hello. I'm Rakkhun.

497
00:36:50,065 --> 00:36:50,945
I love you too.

498
00:36:53,825 --> 00:36:54,905
Vann.

499
00:36:55,545 --> 00:36:56,905
The client's name is Rakkhun.

500
00:36:59,305 --> 00:37:00,545
Sorry.

501
00:37:00,625 --> 00:37:02,385
I thought it was
love at first sight, like…

502
00:37:02,465 --> 00:37:03,985
meeting someone
and blurting out "I love you."

503
00:37:05,825 --> 00:37:06,905
You look familiar.

504
00:37:07,425 --> 00:37:08,865
Have we met before?

505
00:37:16,225 --> 00:37:17,305
I don't want to take this guy's job.

506
00:37:17,905 --> 00:37:21,025
The first time I met him,
I had bad luck all day.

507
00:37:22,345 --> 00:37:24,225
It's nothing. It's an easy job.

508
00:37:24,305 --> 00:37:26,105
The client just wants you to

509
00:37:26,185 --> 00:37:29,385
negotiate with the ghost
that's following him.

510
00:37:29,985 --> 00:37:31,385
I don't believe in that stuff.
You know that.

511
00:37:32,825 --> 00:37:34,985
Sorry, I'm not taking this job.

512
00:37:35,065 --> 00:37:36,105
Calm down, Vann.

513
00:37:36,905 --> 00:37:39,985
For this job,
the client says money is no object.

514
00:37:42,705 --> 00:37:44,545
If you pull it off,

515
00:37:46,105 --> 00:37:48,705
it might pay for your studies
in Japan until you graduate.

516
00:37:53,905 --> 00:37:55,465
I'm willing to pay whatever it takes.

517
00:37:57,225 --> 00:37:59,225
Just get rid of the ghost
that's following me.

518
00:37:59,825 --> 00:38:01,145
I don't want to be single my whole life.

519
00:38:01,225 --> 00:38:03,345
Come on, be serious.

520
00:38:03,425 --> 00:38:05,425
This isn't funny.
What does this have to do with dating?

521
00:38:06,985 --> 00:38:08,385
I've never seen the ghost clearly,

522
00:38:08,985 --> 00:38:10,865
but every person I date gets haunted

523
00:38:11,545 --> 00:38:13,305
until they all disappear from my life.

524
00:38:14,225 --> 00:38:16,305
Please talk to that ghost for me.

525
00:38:16,385 --> 00:38:18,305
Tell it to get out of my life.

526
00:38:18,385 --> 00:38:21,105
But I don't know how or
what to say to drive out a ghost.

527
00:38:21,185 --> 00:38:22,225
Pick someone else.

528
00:38:22,825 --> 00:38:24,265
But the budget for this job
is one million.

529
00:38:30,585 --> 00:38:32,825
Just get rid of the ghost
that's following me,

530
00:38:32,905 --> 00:38:34,465
and the money is yours.

531
00:38:42,425 --> 00:38:43,745
THE CROW CLUB - EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT

532
00:38:50,665 --> 00:38:51,505
I don't like crowds.

533
00:38:52,105 --> 00:38:53,425
At the audition, there'll only be
the label manager

534
00:38:53,505 --> 00:38:54,465
and two board members.

535
00:38:59,145 --> 00:39:00,425
I don't want to be an idol.

536
00:39:00,505 --> 00:39:02,305
When you joined this club,

537
00:39:02,825 --> 00:39:04,545
you said you wouldn't pick
and choose jobs.

538
00:39:08,585 --> 00:39:12,745
Don't you dream
of becoming a singer or musician?

539
00:39:13,865 --> 00:39:17,065
I think going to an audition like this

540
00:39:18,145 --> 00:39:20,745
might bring something new into your life.

541
00:39:41,145 --> 00:39:42,105
Wait!

542
00:39:42,865 --> 00:39:43,705
Hey!

543
00:39:44,345 --> 00:39:45,985
Wait! Hear me out!

544
00:39:47,425 --> 00:39:51,345
I'm asking you
to audition with me just once.

545
00:39:51,945 --> 00:39:53,625
And if our band gets to debut,

546
00:39:53,705 --> 00:39:55,665
then we can talk about the contract later.

547
00:39:57,865 --> 00:39:59,305
I don't like talking to people.

548
00:40:00,465 --> 00:40:03,945
But when you sing,
I don't hear anything else.

549
00:40:04,465 --> 00:40:06,425
I only hear your music and your feelings.

550
00:40:11,105 --> 00:40:12,145
Why?

551
00:40:14,305 --> 00:40:15,305
I don't know.

552
00:40:16,025 --> 00:40:17,785
I've never felt this way before.

553
00:40:18,945 --> 00:40:21,585
Your voice really speaks to my heart.

554
00:40:26,985 --> 00:40:28,505
Aren't you going to greet the client?

555
00:40:28,585 --> 00:40:30,465
This guy is the client?

556
00:40:31,465 --> 00:40:32,905
I don't take clients like him.

557
00:40:33,425 --> 00:40:38,225
Tangmo, talk nicely to your employer.

558
00:40:38,825 --> 00:40:41,985
Sis, you can send me to do construction

559
00:40:42,065 --> 00:40:44,065
or fight the mafia.

560
00:40:45,785 --> 00:40:47,945
But I won't take his job.

561
00:40:48,905 --> 00:40:49,865
Tangmo.

562
00:40:50,665 --> 00:40:54,305
But for this,
you're the only one who can help me.

563
00:40:58,305 --> 00:40:59,745
Why me?

564
00:41:16,905 --> 00:41:18,625
What the fuck do you want from me?

565
00:41:19,665 --> 00:41:23,145
You're the one I believe
can help us win this competition.

566
00:41:24,265 --> 00:41:25,545
I've got the brains.

567
00:41:25,625 --> 00:41:26,705
You've got the strength.

568
00:41:26,785 --> 00:41:28,585
And most importantly, Tangmo,

569
00:41:30,025 --> 00:41:31,465
I want this money.

570
00:41:32,745 --> 00:41:33,785
Money again?

571
00:41:34,825 --> 00:41:36,825
You ran away from your father
to live alone.

572
00:41:36,905 --> 00:41:38,985
You're struggling with money too,
aren't you?

573
00:41:39,745 --> 00:41:41,545
We're talking ten million here.

574
00:41:43,065 --> 00:41:46,105
If we win, I'll give you half.

575
00:41:47,145 --> 00:41:48,945
And I'm ready to sign a contract today.

576
00:41:54,905 --> 00:41:57,865
I'm not desperate enough to team up
and play a game with you again.

577
00:41:59,345 --> 00:42:01,265
You don't want to team up with me…

578
00:42:03,665 --> 00:42:05,385
or is it actually

579
00:42:06,945 --> 00:42:07,945
that you're angry

580
00:42:09,465 --> 00:42:10,785
because you still love me?

581
00:42:10,865 --> 00:42:12,345
You've got some nerve saying that.

582
00:42:12,865 --> 00:42:15,145
If you don't feel anything for me anymore,

583
00:42:16,025 --> 00:42:18,745
just treat this
like any other client's job.

584
00:42:19,785 --> 00:42:21,065
Be professional.

585
00:42:22,745 --> 00:42:24,465
Or do you still refuse to take it…

586
00:42:26,505 --> 00:42:28,065
because deep down,

587
00:42:29,665 --> 00:42:31,905
you still can't move on from me?

588
00:42:37,865 --> 00:42:42,025
THE CROW CLUB - EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT

589
00:42:42,105 --> 00:42:46,265
You want a realistic partner
more perfect than AI,

590
00:42:46,345 --> 00:42:49,985
with the ability to make the client
fall in love for life.

591
00:42:51,185 --> 00:42:54,425
But next to it, it says
it's only until the novel is finished.

592
00:42:56,345 --> 00:43:00,545
But you specified
that you only want Talay.

593
00:43:00,625 --> 00:43:01,865
Yes.

594
00:43:03,025 --> 00:43:07,265
I've decided to use him as the model
for my novel's male lead.

595
00:43:07,865 --> 00:43:09,345
No one else is a good option.

596
00:43:13,065 --> 00:43:14,905
Talay has top-tier experience,

597
00:43:14,985 --> 00:43:16,305
and he's worked here the longest.

598
00:43:16,385 --> 00:43:18,105
Plus, he gets five stars on every case.

599
00:43:18,705 --> 00:43:20,745
He performs impressively at every level.

600
00:43:22,385 --> 00:43:23,625
I understand.

601
00:43:25,025 --> 00:43:27,185
But maybe not.

602
00:43:27,865 --> 00:43:28,705
Why?

603
00:43:29,385 --> 00:43:33,385
Because every Crow has the right
to decide whether to take a job or not.

604
00:43:40,985 --> 00:43:42,345
So, will you take my job?

605
00:43:47,345 --> 00:43:50,505
I get that you're so short on inspiration
you had to hire me.

606
00:43:51,265 --> 00:43:53,065
But I'm sure it won't work.

607
00:43:53,145 --> 00:43:55,585
I'm just using you as a starting point.

608
00:43:55,665 --> 00:43:57,825
I haven't even decided
where the story will go.

609
00:43:58,705 --> 00:44:01,305
Maybe the character "Talay"

610
00:44:01,385 --> 00:44:03,265
might go from someone
who doesn't believe in love

611
00:44:03,785 --> 00:44:06,145
to someone completely consumed by it.

612
00:44:14,145 --> 00:44:15,225
Me?

613
00:44:15,305 --> 00:44:16,905
Consumed by love with you?

614
00:44:17,585 --> 00:44:19,505
I've never been serious about anyone.

615
00:44:19,585 --> 00:44:21,505
And I've never come close to
anything called love.

616
00:44:22,665 --> 00:44:25,945
Why would you bet the future
of your romance novel on me?

617
00:44:27,745 --> 00:44:28,945
I haven't thought that far ahead.

618
00:44:29,465 --> 00:44:31,785
But I'm sure it'll go well.

619
00:44:31,865 --> 00:44:35,465
Because my writer's instinct
is never wrong.

620
00:44:37,305 --> 00:44:40,465
Love isn't something
you can set up, Mr. Writer.

621
00:44:42,065 --> 00:44:45,625
Between two people,
there has to be… chemistry.

622
00:44:46,185 --> 00:44:48,105
Something that makes your heart race.

623
00:44:50,105 --> 00:44:51,265
Which I don't have.

624
00:44:53,265 --> 00:44:55,625
You're saying that without even trying.

625
00:44:55,705 --> 00:44:56,825
That doesn't count.

626
00:45:10,145 --> 00:45:12,665
Well? Feel that chemistry yet?

627
00:45:15,105 --> 00:45:17,025
How could you tell from a test like that?

628
00:45:18,625 --> 00:45:19,745
May I?

629
00:45:58,185 --> 00:46:01,505
I thought a famous romance novelist
would be a better kisser.

630
00:46:03,625 --> 00:46:04,465
Is it clear now?

631
00:46:05,225 --> 00:46:06,825
We have no chemistry.

632
00:46:36,065 --> 00:46:38,345
It's time for me to let the clients know

633
00:46:38,425 --> 00:46:40,505
whether you'll take the jobs.

634
00:46:44,065 --> 00:46:46,105
I don't mind whether you take them or not.

635
00:46:46,705 --> 00:46:50,345
But I always tell you
before you take a job

636
00:46:51,145 --> 00:46:53,465
that a job is a job,

637
00:46:54,945 --> 00:46:58,305
and clients are nothing
more than revenue figures.

638
00:46:59,305 --> 00:47:03,145
If any Crow gets involved with a client,

639
00:47:04,025 --> 00:47:05,465
they'll be fired.

640
00:48:07,385 --> 00:48:09,425
Are you sure that if we put on an act,

641
00:48:09,505 --> 00:48:11,145
that ghost will be
dumb enough to fall for it?

642
00:48:11,225 --> 00:48:13,585
Then you have to make it convincing
enough for the ghost to believe it.

643
00:48:15,825 --> 00:48:18,785
You usually look so dead inside
when talking to clients.

644
00:48:18,865 --> 00:48:20,345
What's gotten into you, Vann?

645
00:48:20,425 --> 00:48:22,505
From now on, when you're sad,
look at this bracelet,

646
00:48:22,585 --> 00:48:23,785
and think of me instead.

647
00:48:23,865 --> 00:48:25,145
Don't think about anyone else.

648
00:48:25,225 --> 00:48:27,465
Rakkhun! We're still together, right?

649
00:48:27,545 --> 00:48:29,305
Kan came to talk to me.

650
00:48:29,905 --> 00:48:31,225
What do you think I should do?

651
00:48:32,425 --> 00:48:33,545
Why are you scared?

652
00:48:33,625 --> 00:48:36,345
The ghost should be scared of me.

